==Russian==
[[Image:Kenyan man 2.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ru|негр}}|upright=1]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|негръ||ru-PRO}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-негр.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|ru|id=negro|:bor|fr:nègre|tree=1}}
{{bor+|ru|fr|nègre}}. Ultimately from {{der|ru|la|niger}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|a=an|f=негритя́нка|adj=негритя́нский}}

# [[black]] (man); [[negro]]
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|offensive|rare}} someone who works for peanuts or for nothing, a slave
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} {{ellipsis of|ru|литерату́рный негр|t=[[ghostwriter]]}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{l|ru|негр}} and {{l|ru|негритя́нка}} are loanwords from French, descending from a Latin root meaning "black." In Russian, these words are traditionally neutral, referring to any person with black skin, and are generally not considered offensive. Nonetheless, some Russian speakers, especially those with knowledge of English, may avoid these words due to their similarity to the English slur.

